# Search Path for Shared Libraries
1.  First checks the directories listed in its Runtime Library Search Path (RPATH), which is embedded within the executable itself.
2.  Looks in the directories specified in the LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable. This variable allows users to define custom library paths without modifying the system-wide configuration.
3.  Similar to RPATH, the Runtime Search Path (RUNPATH) is another directory list embedded in the executable but is checked after LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
4.  The application then checks the directories listed in /etc/ld.so.conf configuration file.
5.  Finally, the search proceeds to the standard system library directories, which include /lib, /lib64, /usr/lib, /usr/lib64.














